          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Work as a Governess</strong><br>\nEmily worked briefly as a teacher and governess but found the experience miserable. She was homesick and disliked being away from the moors. This work did not last long, and she soon returned to the Parsonage to write.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Poetry and Gondal</strong><br>\nTogether with her sisters, Emily published a volume of poetry under pseudonyms to mask their gender. They created an imaginary world called Gondal, for which Emily wrote many poems, although most of the Gondal poems were not published during her lifetime.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"Wuthering Heights\"</strong><br>\nEmily's only novel, \"Wuthering Heights,\" was published in 1847 under the pseudonym Ellis Bell. It is a passionate and tragic tale of love and revenge set on the Yorkshire moors and is considered a classic of English literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
