            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Reception of Her Work</strong><br>\nWuthering Heights received mixed reviews when first published. Some critics admired its originality, while others criticized its dark and brooding character. Over time, it has gained status as a masterpiece with its complex narrative structure and emotional intensity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Health Issues</strong><br>\nEmily's health began to decline during the writing of \"Wuthering Heights.\" She caught cold at her brother's funeral in September 1848, which developed into tuberculosis. Her condition worsened rapidly, and she refused most medical help.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nEmily Brontë died at the age of 30 in December 1848. Her work has had a lasting impact on literature, inspiring countless adaptations and interpretations. She remains a mysterious figure due to her reclusive life and the power of her writing.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
